      <div type="clause" n="42.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 42.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="106" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> hryðera hwelc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.30"/> sie þe hegas brece ⁊ ga in gehwær, ⁊ se hit nolde gehealdan, se hit age oððe ne mæge, nime se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.1-3"/> hit on his æcere mete<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.2-3"/> ⁊ ófslea; ⁊ nime se agenfrigea his fel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.3-3"/> ⁊ flæsc ⁊ þolie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.4-2"/> þæs oðres.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="106" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif þonne hriðera<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.22-2"/> gehwilc sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.3-2"/> ðæt hegas brece ⁊ ga gehwær in, ⁊ se hit nolde gehealden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.23-2"/>, se (þe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.4"/>) hit age oþþe ne mæge, nime se (þe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/>) hit on his æcere gemete ⁊ ofslea; ⁊ nime se agenfriga his flæcs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.2-2"/> and ðolige þæs oðres.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="106" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf ðonne hryðera hwylc sy ðe hégas brece ⁊ ga in gehwær, ⁊ se hit nolde gehealdan, se hit age oððe ne mæge, nime se ðe hit on his æcere gemete ⁊ ofslea; ⁊ nime se agenfriga his flæsc ⁊ ðolie ðæs oðres.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="42.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="107" ed="#liebermann"/>Si uero sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.22"/> animal quod sepes frangat et quolibet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.23"/> introeat, et dominus, cuius animal est, nolit ipsum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.24"/> custodire uel non possit, capiat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.25"/> hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.26"/>, in cuius acra obuiabit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.1"/>, et occidat; et recipiat agenfriga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.2"/> corium eius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.3"/> et carnem et patiatur de cetero.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="50" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif þonne hryðera hwelc<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Ine_42-1.attnote.fn.4"/> sie þe<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_42-1.attnote.fn.5"/> hegas brece ⁊ ga in gehwær, ⁊ se hit nolde gehealdan se hit age oððe ne mæge, nime se hit on his æcere mete<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Ine_42-1.attnote.fn.6"/> ⁊ ófslea, ⁊ nime se agenfrigea his fel ⁊<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Ine_42-1.attnote.fn.7"/> flæsc ⁊ ðolie þæs oðres.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="43.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="406" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> hryðera hwelc sie þe hegas brece ⁊ ga in gehwær, ⁊ se hit nolde gehealdan se hit age oððe ne mæge, nime se hit on his æcere mete ⁊ ófslea; ⁊ nime se agenfrigea his fél ⁊ flæsc ⁊ þolie þæs oðres.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="107" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn [der Schadenstifter] jedoch eines der Rinder ist, das Gehege [gewaltsam] bricht und überall eindringt, da<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.de.1"/> der Eigenthümer es nicht halten wollte oder kann, so nehme [es], wer es auf seinem Acker trifft und erschlage [es]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.de.2"/>; und der Eigenthümer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.de.3"/> erhalte davon Fell<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.de.4"/> und Fleisch und verliere den übrigen [Werth<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_42-1.lnote.de.5"/> des lebendigen Viehs].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if [the cause of the damage] is one of the cattle which [forcibly] breaks the enclosure and gets in everywhere, since its owner would not or cannot keep it in, let whoever finds it on his field take [it] and kill [it]; and let the owner receive its hide and flesh and lose the rest [of the value of the living animal].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="51" ed="#attenborough"/>If, however, any beast breaks hedges and wanders at large within, since its owner will not or cannot keep it under control, he who finds it on his cornland shall take it and kill it. The owner [of the beast] shall take its hide and flesh and suffer the loss of the remainder<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_42-1.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="404" ed="#whitelock"/>If, however, it is any of the cattle which breaks the hedges and enters anywhere, and he who owns it would not or could not control it, he who finds it on his arable is to seize it and kill it; and the owner is to take its hide and flesh and suffer the loss of the rest.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="407" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If, however, it should be one of those heifers that breaks hedges and gets in everywhere, and [the owner] does not wish to or is not able to contain it, let him who finds it on his crop-field take it and kill it; and let the owner take its hide and meat, and forfeit the rest.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="415"><ref target="clause:Ine_50">Ine 50</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_42-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">an. sit <hi rend="italic">HkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">an. sit HkBr</seg></note>
